{"c":[{"id":"b5bfc6a1a409a088","sum":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs): write a new file and mv it over. ScreenModel.apply makes a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot, and candidates.ts/descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-88beaae782960744","text":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs); write a new file and mv it over, as B6 did with run-audit.sh mid-audit.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201045Z-f95178d8fbcf4b52","text":"ScreenModel.apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot; candidates.ts and descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"40c277ae98ccebf5","sum":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame even off screen (perch blink+breath cost 10.9% of a core; one-shot Timer blinks ~1%). The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals, so scripts test == null, not === null.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T213409Z-2c06a8e735f40a5c","text":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame, even through long holds and in a panel never ordered on screen: the perch's 5 s blink plus breath cost the host 10.9% of a core; one-shot blinks on a Timer cost about 1%.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T213409Z-cab3b62b740f0600","text":"The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals (Swift JSONEncoder), so scripts must test == null / undefined, not === null.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
